## General Principles
- Use existing Rose UI components (prefixed with `rs-`) instead of creating new ones
- Customize components through props rather than creating variants
- Follow the established naming conventions and component structure

## Component Usage

### 1. Alert (`<rs-alert>`)
```vue
<rs-alert variant="success" dismissible>Alert message</rs-alert>
```
- **Props**: `variant` (primary/secondary/info/success/warning/danger), `dismissible`, `show`, `autoDismiss`, `timer`

### 2. Badge (`<rs-badge>`)
```vue
<rs-badge variant="primary" icon="ic:baseline-check">Badge text</rs-badge>
```
- **Props**: `variant` (primary/secondary/info/success/warning/danger), `icon`, `iconSize`

### 3. Button (`<rs-button>`)
```vue
<rs-button variant="primary" size="md">Button text</rs-button>
```
- **Props**: `variant` (primary/secondary/info/success/warning/danger + -outline/-text suffixes), `size` (sm/md/lg)

### 4. Card (`<rs-card>`)
```vue
<rs-card>
  <template #header>Card Header</template>
  Card content
  <template #footer>Card Footer</template>
</rs-card>
```
- **Slots**: `header`, `default`, `body`, `footer`

### 5. Collapse (`<rs-collapse>`)
```vue
<rs-collapse accordion type="default">
  <rs-collapse-item title="Item 1">Content 1</rs-collapse-item>
  <rs-collapse-item title="Item 2">Content 2</rs-collapse-item>
</rs-collapse>
```
- **Props**: `accordion`, `type` (default/border)
- **Child Component**: `rs-collapse-item` with `title` prop

### 6. Dropdown (`<rs-dropdown>`)
```vue
<rs-dropdown title="Dropdown" variant="primary" position="bottom">
  <rs-dropdown-item>Option 1</rs-dropdown-item>
  <rs-dropdown-item>Option 2</rs-dropdown-item>
</rs-dropdown>
```
- **Props**: `title`, `variant`, `position` (top/bottom/left/right), `textAlign`, `size`, `itemSize`
- **Child Component**: `rs-dropdown-item` with `divider` prop

### 7. Fieldset (`<rs-fieldset>`)
```vue
<rs-fieldset label="Group Label">
  <FormKit type="text" label="Input 1" />
  <FormKit type="text" label="Input 2" />
</rs-fieldset>
```
- **Props**: `label`, `border`, `borderColour`, `borderWidth`, `borderRadius`

### 8. Modal (`<rs-modal>`)
```vue
<rs-modal v-model="showModal" title="Modal Title" size="md">
  Modal content
  <template #footer>Custom footer</template>
</rs-modal>
```
- **Props**: `title`, `size` (sm/md/lg), `position` (top/center/bottom), `hideOverlay`, `okOnly`, `cancelOnly`, `okTitle`, `cancelTitle`, `okCallback`, `cancelCallback`, `hideFooter`, `overlayClose`, `height`
- **Slots**: `header`, `body` (default), `footer`

### 9. Progress Bar (`<rs-progress-bar>`)
```vue
<rs-progress-bar label="Progress" value="75" max="100" variant="primary" size="md" showValue />
```
- **Props**: `label`, `value`, `max`, `variant`, `size` (sm/md/lg), `showValue`

### 10. Tab (`<rs-tab>`)
```vue
<rs-tab variant="primary" type="default" vertical fill>
  <rs-tab-item title="Tab 1">Content 1</rs-tab-item>
  <rs-tab-item title="Tab 2">Content 2</rs-tab-item>
</rs-tab>
```
- **Props**: `variant`, `type` (default/card/border), `vertical`, `fill`, `justify` (left/center/right)
- **Child Component**: `rs-tab-item` with `title` prop

### 11. Table (`<rs-table>`)
```vue
<rs-table 
  :field="['ID', 'Name', 'Email']" 
  :data="tableData"
  :options="{ variant: 'default', striped: true, hover: true }"
  :optionsAdvanced="{ sortable: true, filterable: true }"
/>
```
- **Props**: 
  - `field`: Column headers
  - `data`: Table data
  - `options`: { variant, striped, bordered, borderless, hover }
  - `optionsAdvanced`: { sortable, filterable, responsive, outsideBorder }
  - `pageSize`, `grid`

### 12. Wizard (`<rs-wizard>`)
```vue
<rs-wizard :steps="['Step 1', 'Step 2']" type="top">
  <template #step1>
    <FormKit type="text" label="Step 1 Field" validation="required" />
  </template>
  <template #step2>
    <FormKit type="text" label="Step 2 Field" validation="required" />
  </template>
</rs-wizard>
```
- **Props**: `type` (top/left), `steps`, `currentStep`, `form`, `formSubmit`, `formAction`, `formStepRequired`, `formStepBack`, `formNavigate`, `formErrorCounter`
- **Slots**: Named slots for each step (lowercase, no spaces)

### 13. Code Mirror (`<rs-code-mirror>`)
```vue
<rs-code-mirror v-model="code" mode="vue" height="70vh" theme="oneDark" />
```
- **Props**: `modelValue`, `mode` (vue/javascript), `height`, `theme`, `disabled`, `options` 